---
import Doc from '../layouts/Doc.astro';
import SiteLink from '../components/SiteLink.astro';
import { APP_NAME, BUSINESS_NAME, SUPPORT_EMAIL } from '../utils/env';

const effectiveDateISO = '2026-04-23';
const effectiveDateLabel = 'April 23, 2026';
---

<Doc
  title="Terms"
  description={`Terms of Service for ${APP_NAME}. Acceptable use, IP, New Jersey governing law.`}
>
  <header class="doc__header">
    <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
  </header>

  <p>
    These Terms govern your use of {APP_NAME}. By using the app, you agree to these Terms. If you do not agree, do not use the app.
  </p>

  <section>
    <h2>What you can do</h2>
    <p>
      {APP_NAME} lets you draw pictures inside Messages and send them to the people you choose.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What you cannot do</h2>
    <p>You agree not to use {APP_NAME} to create or send content that is:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Unlawful, harassing, threatening, or defamatory</li>
      <li>Sexually explicit, obscene, or that exploits or endangers minors</li>
      <li>Hateful, or intended to harass or intimidate a specific person or group</li>
      <li>Infringing any third party's copyright, trademark, right of publicity, or other intellectual property</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Your drawings</h2>
    <p>
      You own what you draw. {BUSINESS_NAME} claims no ownership of, and no license to, your drawings. {BUSINESS_NAME} does not store, transmit, monitor, moderate, or pre-screen drawings. Drawings travel directly between sender and recipient through Apple's iMessage service; {BUSINESS_NAME}'s infrastructure never processes drawing content. You are solely responsible for drawings you create and send, and for drawings you choose to view.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Our property</h2>
    <p>
      The {APP_NAME} name, app, word packs, artwork, and software are the property of {BUSINESS_NAME}. These Terms grant no other rights.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Warranties and liability</h2>
    <p class="doc__caps">
      The app is provided "as is" and "as available," with all faults, and without warranty of any kind. To the maximum extent permitted by law, {BUSINESS_NAME} disclaims all warranties, express or implied, including the implied warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and non-infringement.
    </p>
    <p class="doc__caps">
      To the maximum extent permitted by law, {BUSINESS_NAME} will not be liable for any indirect, incidental, consequential, special, exemplary, or punitive damages arising from or related to your use of the app, even if advised of the possibility of such damages. {BUSINESS_NAME}'s total liability for any claim arising out of or related to the app will not exceed fifty U.S. dollars (US$50).
    </p>
    <p>
      Some jurisdictions do not allow the exclusion of implied warranties or the limitation of certain damages, so some of the above may not apply to you. Nothing in these Terms limits any rights or remedies you may have under the New Jersey Consumer Fraud Act, N.J.S.A. 56:8-1 et seq., or any other right that cannot be waived or limited under applicable law. For New Jersey residents, the exclusions and limitations above do not apply to the extent they would limit any non-waivable rights under New Jersey law.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Indemnification</h2>
    <p>
      You will indemnify and hold {BUSINESS_NAME} harmless from any third-party claim, loss, or expense (including reasonable attorneys' fees) arising from (a) drawings or content you create, send, or share using the app; (b) your breach of these Terms; or (c) your violation of any law or third-party right.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      {BUSINESS_NAME} may update these Terms. Updates apply prospectively only. For material changes, {BUSINESS_NAME} will update the effective date and provide notice in the app at least thirty (30) days before they take effect. Your continued use of the app after that date constitutes acceptance of the updated Terms. If you do not agree, stop using the app.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Integration</h2>
    <p>
      These Terms, together with Apple's Licensed Application End User License Agreement (or the Custom End User License Agreement accepted at install) and the {APP_NAME} <SiteLink href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</SiteLink>, constitute the entire agreement between you and {BUSINESS_NAME} regarding the app. If these Terms conflict with Apple's End User License Agreement on matters it addresses, Apple's agreement controls.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Apple as third-party beneficiary</h2>
    <p>
      Apple Inc. and its subsidiaries are third-party beneficiaries of these Terms and may enforce them against you. Except for Apple, no other person or entity is a third-party beneficiary of these Terms.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Governing law</h2>
    <p>
      These Terms are governed by the laws of the State of New Jersey, without regard to conflict-of-laws principles. Any dispute arising from these Terms or your use of {APP_NAME} shall be resolved exclusively in the state or federal courts located in New Jersey.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Termination</h2>
    <p>
      {BUSINESS_NAME} may revoke your license to use the app for any breach of these Terms. These Terms terminate automatically if you uninstall the app. Sections on ownership, indemnification, disclaimers, limitations, governing law, and dispute resolution survive termination.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Severability and assignment</h2>
    <p>
      If any provision of these Terms is held unenforceable, the remaining provisions remain in effect, and the unenforceable provision will be modified to the minimum extent necessary to make it enforceable. {BUSINESS_NAME} may assign these Terms without notice or consent. You may not assign these Terms without {BUSINESS_NAME}'s prior written consent.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Export controls</h2>
    <p>
      You represent that you are not located in any country subject to U.S. Government embargo or designated as a terrorist-supporting country, and that you are not on any U.S. Government list of prohibited or restricted parties.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Age</h2>
    <p>
      The app is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly allow use by children under 13. By using the app you represent that you are at least 13, or that a parent or guardian has agreed to these Terms on your behalf.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Notice and limitations period</h2>
    <p>
      Notices to {BUSINESS_NAME} must be sent to <SiteLink href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</SiteLink>. Any claim arising out of the app must be filed within two (2) years after it arises, except where a longer period is non-waivable under applicable law.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Intellectual-property complaints</h2>
    <p>
      For intellectual-property complaints about content transmitted through the app, contact <SiteLink href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</SiteLink> with a description of the claim, the allegedly infringing material, and your contact information.
    </p>
  </section>

  <footer class="doc__meta">Effective <time datetime={effectiveDateISO}>{effectiveDateLabel}</time></footer>
</Doc>

<style>
  .doc__caps {
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
  }
</style>
